    "intro_narrative": "The irradiated winds howl across the desolate wasteland, stripping the paint from the armored doors of Outpost Echo. For months, you have chased the rumors of this buried pre-war military bunker, which supposedly holds the encrypted coordinates to Eden—the last known uncorrupted sanctuary on Earth. As you pry open the maintenance hatch and drop into the darkness, the air is thick with the smell of ozone, rust, and decay. The heavy main blast doors are firmly sealed, controlled by an array of dormant, dust-covered technology left behind by the old-world engineers. The geiger counter at your hip is ticking faster, warning you that a massive rad-storm is fast approaching. To unlock the final coordinates and secure your passage to the sanctuary, you must trace the fragmented data pathways and decipher the automated security protocols. Your survival depends on making these ancient machines speak to each other once more.",
    "narrative_style": "post_apocalyptic"
  },
